Z||000024||BN Boomer||11-11-2001||12:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>No-one's being anti-war... But the US acting out their aggression on civilian targets... That's terrorism. NO BETTER than what happened in NY. <P>At the moment, things are moving nicely. The Taliban is falling like mown grass, and Civilian casualties are minimal.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Where's your proof that we are "acting out our aggression on civilian targets"? Please don't tell me that you are one of those morons who think that because the US has developed some high tech precision weapons there should be no collateral damage. They don't call it "The Fog of War" for nothing.  <P>Are you even aware that those two statements totally contradict each other? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||Mach10||11-11-2001||01:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B> Where's your proof that we are "acting out our aggression on civilian targets"? Please don't tell me that you are one of those morons who think that because the US has developed some high tech precision weapons there should be no collateral damage. They don't call it "The Fog of War" for nothing.  <P>Are you even aware that those two statements totally contradict each other? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Where do you see me claiming that the US is targetting Civilians?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Re-read the post... <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000026||JohnnyK||11-11-2001||02:43 AM||||It's kind of odd to watch how all of you were of the same mentality before "Kill them all. Nuke them! Carpet bomb them with tac nukes. They need a nuclear winter." etc, but now since people are actually dying, a lot (most) of you have changed your tune.||||reg||1
Z||000027||maryjane||11-11-2001||06:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>It's kind of odd to watch how all of you were of the same mentality before "Kill them all. Nuke them! Carpet bomb them with tac nukes. They need a nuclear winter." etc, but now since people are actually dying, a lot (most) of you have changed your tune.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Johnny,<BR>What you are seeing as a change in tune, is actually that. But it is not a change in thought or beliefs. PC, exists even here on PFF. If people always posted what they really thought, flame wars would never stop.<BR>Often , for obvious reasons, it is best to appear to be patient, understanding, & compassionate. I'm guilty of it myself.People forget too quickly here in this country. It stems from our ability to carry out a war action somewhere and yet still go about our daily routines of making a living and keeping our same std of living. <BR>The shock of 9-11 has worn off, the attack , as bad as it was, wasn't diverse enough in location to affect too many for the long haul. You can bet they haven't forgotten about it in NYC tho.<BR>Had the attacks been spread out accross NY, Chicago, LA, New Orleans, Saint Louis for instance, It would have DIRECTLY affected all geographical areas and we would be at real war, not 'precision, boys, we don't want to hurt anybody innocent'. I might as well say it for the record. "Had we nuked them on the 12th of SEPT, most of the protests would have died down by now, & nobody else would be willing to harbor terrorist in their country for a long time."<BR>Quoted part is my deep down, gut level belief. It is also why they won't let Don run things for a couple days.||||reg||1
