sive assholes...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>True and true<BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Soon as the Taliban is "exterminated" maybe life can get back to normal EVERYWHERE in the world (we can only wish it does).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I don't think anything will ever be the same for mankind. Everything and everyone must now be viewed as a potential weapon and target, even the most unconceivable things. The White House, a delivery truck, a city hall, a motor cycle. Nothing will be the same.<P><BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>"Now the big bad wolf , the USAF is raining down harsh anal justice from 35,000ft" Reminds me of the email I got. Put all the rubble from the WTC, huge concrete chunks, steel, appliances, desks, in C-130's & C-5's and drop it all over Afganistan from 30,000ft. A Fridgedaire can do a lot of damage from that high up. Headlines would read: WORLD TRADE CENTER STRIKES BACK!! We could claim it's humanitarian, lend-lease donations. For that matter, we could divert all U.S. mail for a week and drop it all over the country. They'd be so afraid of getting anthrax, they'd surrender in a week.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>There ya go a humanitarian way of ending the war.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>It's kind of odd to watch how all of you were of the same mentality before "Kill them all. Nuke them! Carpet bomb them with tac nukes. They need a nuclear winter." etc, but now since people are actually dying, a lot (most) of you have changed your tune.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was in favor of it before and I'm still in favored of it now even if it means collateral damage from radiation here in the states. It's best we deal with the situation in a permanent manner before they deal with us in a permanent manner. Think 9-11 was bad? Image in the headline:"...Washington is gone I mean complete obliterated. It it it looks like someone set of a nucular weapon here! With congress in session and the president and vice president meeting with Israelite leader in the White House all dead our country in now leaderless. Governmnet around the world are mobilizing there armed forces, peopel are buying everthing from the stores. Massive injuries are being reported around the world from peopel rushing to the stores and fighting over food and water..."<BR>Think they wouldn't do it? We never conceived they would run planes into the WTC either.<P>maryjane, your right. People in this country have a short attention span. I blame it one the news. I think the news could be instrumental in helping us out to be better people but the government would rather let it continue to degrade our standards of other by constantly showing murders/rapes/violent crimes as there top stories? Yea someone died last night 'cause someone else was a as$hole. Ok. Now what about the local college plays. Anyway, where was I?<P>   Maybe I'm alone here but I'm a patriot dam* it. I'll die for my neighbor if it comes to that. These Taliban f*cks are militant b*tchs deserving of some old fashion wrath. I'm not agenst them believing whatever they want but there human right end there my face begin. They kill my neighbor I'm ganna come after them na make there life a living h*ll. Cut there b*lls off and see how they treat women after that.<P>"...nuke 'em till they glow them shoot 'em in the dark." and "Temporary problem, permanant solution." Either way well never have to deal with them again.<P>My $.02<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed.<BR>"The car formerly know as Dj's Fiero."<p>[This message has been edited by Pheagey (edited 11-11-2001).]||||reg||1
