Z||000035||Return of Fiero||11-12-2001||01:41 PM||||First thing is if you have a weak stomach, please do not continue to read my post. i would feel horibal if someone got sick from reading this. <P>Next if you dont mind me taking the focus off the "war" and on to a more personal matter, i have a question about desinsitization of the average US citezen.<P>Back a few years ago, there was a major accedent involving 2 trailor trucks and a few cars. one car, the one causeing the accedent, bounced off the two trailors, and one of them fliped onto the car. the car was about 6 inchs high after being crushed, and the two passengers were slightly thiner than that. as i was driving over the rise, i saw the truck flipping on to the car, and i hit the brakes, but from where i was on the highway i saw another car nail the flipped trailor. when i got into the area of the highway that was now a parking lot, i jumped out of my car and ran to the accedent to see if i could do anything. when i got to the car that hit the trailor, i noticed the guy inside was still stirring, and also the car was burning. as i was afraid the guy might be blow up if the car exploded, i tried to help him out of the car. He was babling, but he had stopped talking about 30 seconds after i got to him. it wasnt easy to get him out, as everything was pushed forward, and the engine pushed back, there was no room to manuver, but i thought i could get the guy out. as i was strugleing, another man came over and yelled, "let me help, its going to blow!" and helped pull. we go the guy out of the car, and i realized why he stopped talking, the mans leg was still in the car. i had enough time to look back in the car, see a dark liquid pool in the front seat, and a human leg with pants still attached. the weirdest thing about this is it never phased me, not one bit. not even when i washed the blood off me, or took my blood stained clothes off. it didnt bother me i was carrying a dead man, seeing his leg in the car, or him away from his leg. i dont know if this is normal, or if this is just being desensitized, but the first post made me think of this. is this the product of too many horror, action movies? is this the effect of watching fake items on TV and movies, or rather a persons body deciding to blak out the emotions involed with such a tramatic sight? i only ask because i feel like its not human to have no emotions toward this, and want to know if this seems normal.<P>sorry so long,<BR>Myke<P> ||||reg||1
